From 13dafd7a63e8b12a3d22ac28d40d2644544af9f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:12:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 119/121] net: ipa: add Kaanapali support

Kaanapali has IPA v5.5 like SM8550, but its configuration differs, as
seen in the downstream driver:

 - AP LAN RX, AP modem RX and modem AP RX use endpoints 17, 24 and 22
   (GSI channels 14, 1 and 7)
 - up to 12 outstanding DDR writes (16 reads, the hardware maximum)
 - its own local memory layout, with the microcontroller regions at the
   start and the tables from 0x408
 - IMEM at 0x14683000 and a 0x19000 byte SMEM region
 - modem GSI channels 0-8 to halt after the modem stops

The SM8550 endpoint numbers address other endpoints on Kaanapali, and
mobile data only works with all of the above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
